From 862c003021908c0b89deeb1a38f67affc4be648d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sam Elliott <aelliott@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:03:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [RISCV][compiler-rt] Asm funcs should be hidden

The C builtins are built with `-fvisibility=hidden` when that option is
available, as the builtins are expected to be statically linked and not
called across shared library boundaries.

Before this change, the assembly-written builtin implementations were
declared with STV_DEFAULT visibility, meaning they would be visible
across shared library boundaries. This change moves them to being
declared as STV_HIDDEN to fix this issue.

In particular, the save/restore routines are not normal functions and
cannot be called via a PLT, so this fixes a bug there, and also applies
it to the assembly multiply routine.
